# Question 1 — Cell Membranes and Diffusion
Total: 5 marks

## 1(a) — 1 mark

Focus: Identify the membrane property allowing an amoeba to change shape.

Marking point:
- The membrane is fluid.
- Accept movement of phospholipids or proteins within the membrane.

Examiner notes:
- "Flexible" alone is insufficient.
- "Fluid mosaic model" alone does not earn the mark.

## 1(b)(i) — 1 mark

Correct option: A

- Surface area = 90,000π μm².
- Use the radius, not the diameter.
- Surface area must have squared units.

## 1(b)(ii) — 1 mark

Correct option: C

- Surface area increases.
- Volume remains unchanged.

## 1(b)(iii) — 2 marks

Focus: Explain why an amoeba obtains enough oxygen by diffusion.

Award two distinct points:
- Oxygen concentration or partial pressure is higher outside the cell.
- Its small size produces a short diffusion distance.
- Its relatively large surface-area-to-volume ratio supports diffusion.
- Its metabolic oxygen requirement is relatively low.

